<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2402" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ămȳmōnē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμυμώνη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Daughter of Danăus</i>, <i>and grandmother of Palamedes</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				169</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 3, 22, 27</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A fountain near Argos</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2,
				240</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ămȳmōnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>pertaining to
			Amymone</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 169</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
